var(--muted);font-size:1rem}@media (max-width:699px){.c3-glance{gap:.3rem}.c3-glance li{flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-start;text-align:center;gap:.2rem;padding:.4rem .1rem}.c3-glance .i{width:1.6rem;height:1.6rem}.c3-glance strong{font-size:.875rem}.c3-glance span.t{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.2}}</style><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>5,277 new homes</strong><span class="t">sold by builders in Horry County in 12 months</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5.5 7h8A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 15 8.5v11a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5h-8A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-11A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 5.5 7zM8 7V4.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 9.5 3h9A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 20 4.5v11a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5H15M9.5 17.5l-2.3-2.4a1.4 1.4 0 0 1 2.3-1.6 1.4 1.4 0 0 1 2.3 1.6z"/></svg></span><span><strong>16 builders</strong><span class="t">sold 50 or more each</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>About $335,000</strong><span class="t">middle price of a builder's new home</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Counted from county deeds: every builder that sold 50 or more new homes in a year, the towns it builds in and what its homes cost.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">D.R. Horton and Lennar build the most new homes around Myrtle Beach. Together they sold about 45 percent of the 5,277 new homes builders sold in Horry County in the 12 months to October 2026.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ryan Homes, Pulte Homes and Meritage Homes come next, and 16 builders sold 50 or more. We counted homes sold in county deeds. We do not rate build quality.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">About 1,090 new homes are for sale now. We send you the ones that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send us your town and price</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#ranking" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who builds the most</a></li><li><a href="#where" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where they build</a></li><li><a href="#prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What they cost</a></li><li><a href="#owners" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who owns which name</a></li><li><a href="#warranty" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Warranty and lender</a></li><li><a href="#ask" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Before you sign</a></li><li><a href="#new-home-builders-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">New home builders FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="ranking"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who builds the most">Which builders build the most new homes around Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">D.R. Horton sold the most, about 1 in 4 of the new homes builders sold here. Each bar is one builder, with the middle price its buyers paid:</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="New homes each builder sold to a first owner in Horry County"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">New homes each builder sold to a first owner in Horry County</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Builder, middle price</span><span role="columnheader">homes sold</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">D.R. Horton</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $325,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">1,397</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Lennar</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $258,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.692" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">967</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ryan Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $350,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.341" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">477</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pulte Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $488,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.273" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">382</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Meritage Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $340,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.224" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">313</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Five community companies</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $526,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.171" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">239</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mungo Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $396,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.147" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">206</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Great Southern Homes, now Stanley Martin</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $326,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.13" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">182</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Beverly Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $324,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.13" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">182</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Beazer Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $393,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.112" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">156</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Dream Finders Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $309,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.107" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">149</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Starlight Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $259,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.106" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">148</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Toll Brothers</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $612,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.072" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ashton Woods</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $380,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.067" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">94</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">DRB Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $327,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.044" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">61</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Howell Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $318,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.037" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">52</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Our count of county deeds recorded November 2025 to October 2026: houses, townhouses and condos a builder sold to its first owner. Builders that sold 50 or more. The middle price is the one half sold above and half below.</figcaption></figure><div class="bd-side bd-side-photo"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The five largest sold about two-thirds of the builders' homes. The other builders we counted in the county's deeds each sold fewer than 50.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders sold about 3 in 10 of the 17,774 residential sales recorded, a count that also takes in some lot and land sales. A builder's new home sold for about $335,000 in the middle, against about $306,000 for a home resold by its owner.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">D.R. Horton's pace rose through the year: 569 sales from November to April, then 828 from May to October.</p><figure class="bd-photo"><img src="/images/2026-11-n/buyers-builders/auberon-woods-land-before-building-2023-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-n/buyers-builders/auberon-woods-land-before-building-2023-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-n/buyers-builders/auberon-woods-land-before-building-2023-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1099px) 100vw, 340px" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Aerial view of cleared woodland and bare graded ground with new dirt roads and ponds, surrounded by pine woods, with no houses yet"><figcaption>Part of Auberon Woods in Conway from above, in the 2023 government aerial photo. D.R. Horton sold 176 new homes inside this frame in the 12 months we counted.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where they build">Where does each builder build in Horry County?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Mostly inland, in three mailing towns. Conway, Longs and Myrtle Beach addresses took about 3 in 4 of the new homes builders sold:</p><figure class="bd-map"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 430" role="img